< - "morphemes": the name split into its meaningful members, each in stem form, IAST, lowercase. A compound name gives its members (Viśvāmitra -> ["viśva", "mitra"]; Divodāsa -> ["divas", "dāsa"]; Trasadasyu -> ["trasa", "dasyu"]). A simple name gives one member (["indra"]). Give the same member the same spelling every time it occurs. Drop patronymic and descent-marking suffixes and the vowel strengthening that goes with them: give the base name (Bhārgava -> ["bhṛgu"], Kāṇva -> ["kaṇva"]); if the base name is already in the list as its own entry, leave the patronymic form out. Do not split a name whose analysis is unknown or disputed; give it whole.
< - "gloss": a few English words for the meaning of each member, in order, separated by " + " (for example "all + friend"). Use "name" for a member with no known meaning.
< - "source": "rigveda" or "vedic".
